---
id: skillet-blistered-green-beans
title: Skillet-Blistered Frozen Whole Green Beans
category: modular_cooked_veg

yield:
  servings: 2
  cooked_g: 420

storage:
  fridge_days: 4
  freezer_friendly: true

---

Place @frozen-green-beans{1%package} in a large #skillet with 30 ml of water. Cover tightly with a lid and heat over medium-high for ~steam-time{4.5%min} until fully thawed and tender-crisp.

Remove the lid and turn the heat to high. Allow any remaining water to boil off completely (~evaporate-time{1%min}).

Once the pan is clear of moisture, drizzle @avocado-oil{2%tsp} directly over the beans. Season evenly with @kosher-salt{0.5%tsp}, @garlic-powder{0.33%tsp}, and @black-pepper{0.25%tsp}. Sauté undisturbed for ~sear-time{2.5%min}, tossing occasionally, to blister the exterior skins.

Divide equally into 2 meal prep containers (210 g cooked yield each) and let cool before sealing.
